# 5. ARCHITECTURAL CONTRACT

The project uses a role-first, feature-colocated architecture.

The established structure is:

```text
src/
├── components/
│   ├── admin/
│   ├── staff/
│   ├── secretary/
│   ├── public/
│   ├── auth/
│   ├── layout/
│   ├── shared/
│   └── ui/
│
├── pages/
│   ├── admin/
│   ├── staff/
│   ├── secretary/
│   └── public/
│
├── hooks/
│   ├── admin/
│   ├── staff/
│   ├── secretary/
│   └── public/
│
├── lib/
│   ├── api/
│   ├── auth/
│   ├── session/
│   ├── cookies/
│   ├── env/
│   ├── query/
│   └── <role>/<feature>/
│
├── layouts/
├── routes/
├── providers/
├── contexts/
├── store/
├── types/
├── constant/
├── motion/
└── styles/
```

Do not introduce alternative architectural structures unless explicitly requested.

Do NOT introduce:

* `features/` as a replacement architecture.
* A new `services/` layer.
* Redux or another state-management system.
* A second API client.
* A second router.
* A second authentication mechanism.
* Duplicate query infrastructure.
* Duplicate provider systems.
* Unnecessary global abstractions.

