# 38. DEFINITION OF DONE

A feature is considered complete when:

* The real backend contract is respected.
* Existing architecture is preserved.
* Correct API functions exist.
* React Query is used correctly for server state.
* Types are strict.
* Routes are correctly registered and lazy-loaded.
* Authorization is correctly integrated.
* Loading/empty/error/success states are handled.
* UI is responsive and accessible.
* No unnecessary dependencies were added.
* No unrelated code was changed.
* Relevant verification passes.
* The implementation is production-oriented.

---

# 39. FINAL ENGINEERING PRINCIPLE

Always optimize for:

```text
Correctness
    >
Architectural consistency
    >
Security
    >
Maintainability
    >
Simplicity
    >
Performance
    >
Visual polish
```

while satisfying the actual product requirement.

The best implementation is not the largest or most sophisticated one.

It is the **smallest correct, maintainable, secure implementation that fits the existing architecture and real backend contract.**

When in doubt:

```text
Search first.
Read only what matters.
Reuse what exists.
Do not guess.
Change the minimum.
Verify the result.
